WEBVTT

00:30.001 --> 00:32.421
That feels so good.

00:32.511 --> 00:35.181
I'm going to wash off all my fleas and lice.

00:37.391 --> 00:39.931
Hey. Don't just sit there in the corner.

00:40.011 --> 00:41.101
Come over here.

00:41.181 --> 00:44.061
You'll be eaten by a sea serpent if you fall in.

00:47.811 --> 00:49.401
He's ignoring me?

00:49.481 --> 00:51.361
He's no fun.

00:55.911 --> 00:56.911
In the Middle Ages,

00:58.031 --> 01:00.911
Danes living in Denmark

01:00.991 --> 01:05.921
who made a living as pirates, or thieves,
were known as Vikings.

01:11.881 --> 01:15.631
The Vikings had always longed
to live in England,

01:15.721 --> 01:17.721
a vast and fertile land.

01:19.551 --> 01:23.971
At the start of the ninth century,
the Vikings invaded England,

01:24.061 --> 01:28.941
and migrated into the northern region
as they expanded their power.

01:30.231 --> 01:32.941
However, in 1002 AD...

01:33.031 --> 01:33.861
Kill them all.

01:33.941 --> 01:36.951
the English army attacked the Vikings
who had immigrated there.

01:38.361 --> 01:40.741
In retaliation,

01:40.831 --> 01:46.461
Denmark began to dispatch troops to England,
and intensified its attacks.

01:50.331 --> 01:52.711
Following these political developments,

01:52.801 --> 01:57.131
the Vikings were thrust into a war

01:57.221 --> 02:00.391
to subdue the English army.

03:37.521 --> 03:40.441
THE JOURNEY BEGINS

03:41.321 --> 03:42.491
Don't stop.

03:42.571 --> 03:43.951
Keep moving.

03:44.031 --> 03:44.951
Shut up.

03:45.491 --> 03:46.831
I'm rowing, see?

03:50.001 --> 03:52.081
They went out with a big bang.

03:58.171 --> 04:00.761
All right. Let's stop here.

04:00.841 --> 04:02.421
Stop the ship.

04:04.091 --> 04:06.181
VICINITY OF GAINSBOROUGH
THE CENTER OF ENGLAND

04:06.851 --> 04:09.681
What a pain. It's so hard to walk.

04:10.721 --> 04:13.191
And it smells terrible.

04:36.881 --> 04:37.711
Damn.

04:40.001 --> 04:42.881
These guys aren't army regulars, are they?

04:42.971 --> 04:46.591
The Danish army hires guys like us
for their own army.

04:46.681 --> 04:48.221
The Danish army?

04:48.721 --> 04:52.061
Are the Vikings helping in the war?

04:52.141 --> 04:56.191
Yeah, skirmishes with the English army
are breaking out all over the place.

04:56.271 --> 04:58.981
Vikings are incredible tools of war.

05:00.071 --> 05:04.861
The King of Denmark is going
to invade England someday.

05:04.951 --> 05:08.411
I don't know when it's going to happen,
but they're laying the groundwork now.

05:09.451 --> 05:12.871
You mean they're eliminating people
who stand in the way

05:12.951 --> 05:14.831
before the king sets foot on shore.

05:14.911 --> 05:16.251
That's right.

05:16.331 --> 05:17.831
If we assist,

05:18.961 --> 05:20.881
we'll be compensated well.

05:30.471 --> 05:32.391
There's so many bugs here.

05:32.471 --> 05:33.851
It's better than being cold.

05:33.931 --> 05:36.391
We got to earn a lot this time of year.

05:43.901 --> 05:46.321
Hey. Not bad, right?

05:49.451 --> 05:50.531
You're right.

05:50.621 --> 05:54.751
The English troops harbored by the lord
of this region are giving us a hard time.

05:54.831 --> 05:56.711
I have more than a hundred soldiers.

05:57.211 --> 06:00.251
My forces are greater than yours.

06:01.501 --> 06:03.711
The pirate's talking big.

06:03.801 --> 06:05.711
Don't say that.

06:06.261 --> 06:08.091
We're both Danes.

06:08.181 --> 06:10.261
Don't act as if we're the same.

06:12.011 --> 06:13.311
What did you say?

06:15.771 --> 06:17.271
Well, well.

06:17.351 --> 06:20.351
They're going to invade with full force
in coming years.

06:21.021 --> 06:25.361
In that case,
I think it'd be smart to move fast.

06:25.441 --> 06:28.031
None of you will die anyway.

06:29.991 --> 06:31.411
So, what do you want?

06:32.241 --> 06:34.161
Seven pounds of gold.

06:34.241 --> 06:36.911
And all the treasure and food the lord has.

06:37.001 --> 06:38.831
And we're taking all the women.

06:40.921 --> 06:42.251
Five pounds.

06:42.331 --> 06:44.171
As for the rest, it's yours.

06:46.711 --> 06:49.051
It's decided. Deal.

06:51.931 --> 06:54.391
What? What are they talking about?

06:54.471 --> 06:57.181
A job. They closed the deal.

06:57.271 --> 07:00.141
Great. Then it's time to eat.

07:01.561 --> 07:05.151
Well, then.
I will send another messenger tomorrow.

07:05.231 --> 07:07.441
I'll leave the battle plans to you.

07:07.531 --> 07:08.901
Don't run away.

07:08.991 --> 07:11.281
You have nowhere to retreat.

07:12.911 --> 07:14.911
And don't try anything funny.

07:22.831 --> 07:24.671
They surrounded us.

07:27.421 --> 07:28.461
Hey. Ear.

07:28.551 --> 07:30.221
You're so loud.

07:30.301 --> 07:31.931
Shoot. Shoot.

07:34.681 --> 07:35.931
It hit my ass.

07:43.191 --> 07:45.111
This will be good exercise after dinner.

07:45.191 --> 07:46.021
Kill them.

07:46.771 --> 07:48.531
Beat them at their own game.

07:51.701 --> 07:52.911
Shoot. Shoot.

07:57.871 --> 07:59.121
Damn.

08:10.461 --> 08:12.801
Try achieving something great on the battlefield.

08:13.471 --> 08:17.681
Then I'll reward you with a duel.

08:22.601 --> 08:24.441
Something great...

08:28.021 --> 08:29.191
Kid.

08:29.611 --> 08:30.941
Are you a pirate too?

08:43.541 --> 08:46.631
If you're angry, blame it on the blood of the Danes.

08:58.971 --> 09:01.101
Sorry. I didn't know you were alive.

09:03.181 --> 09:05.811
On the battlefield, the weak die first.

09:07.151 --> 09:08.561
Like you.

09:13.571 --> 09:14.401
Damn.

09:33.381 --> 09:35.221
Damn kid.

09:35.301 --> 09:37.181
Die.

11:12.521 --> 11:14.231
You bastard.

11:23.571 --> 11:25.701
You're starting to look like a fighter.

11:39.171 --> 11:40.761
Hey, Thorfinn.

11:40.841 --> 11:42.971
Can you go scout for a bit?

11:43.971 --> 11:46.261
What? Why do I have to go?

12:02.321 --> 12:04.111
Kid. How dare you?

12:06.411 --> 12:07.871
Hold him down.

12:07.951 --> 12:09.331
I'm going to kill him.

12:36.101 --> 12:37.061
There he is.

12:37.151 --> 12:38.521
Over there.

12:58.041 --> 12:59.961
Over there. Don't let him get away.

13:21.901 --> 13:25.991
You know, I think the present king is a fool.

13:26.071 --> 13:29.121
Mom. Don't say that out loud.

13:29.201 --> 13:32.161
King Edgar from two generations ago was good.

13:32.241 --> 13:34.291
He made friends with the Danes.

13:35.331 --> 13:37.751
Everyone respected him.

13:37.831 --> 13:40.421
He was a good Christian.

13:42.961 --> 13:46.301
But the reigning king, King Ethelred, is no good.

13:46.381 --> 13:50.101
He suddenly killed all the Danes in the country.

13:51.681 --> 13:54.471
Of course they'd be mad.

13:54.561 --> 13:55.641
Mom.

13:55.731 --> 13:58.901
Don't say that in front of other people.

13:58.981 --> 14:01.521
If a soldier overheard you...

14:04.611 --> 14:07.321
Mom. Come over here. Mom.

14:09.951 --> 14:13.951
1008 AD
EAST ANGLIA THE EAST OF ENGLAND

14:42.861 --> 14:43.821
You're awake.

14:45.571 --> 14:48.651
We were just about to eat dinner.

14:48.741 --> 14:50.361
How are your wounds?

14:52.201 --> 14:54.531
I washed your clothes.

14:54.621 --> 14:56.081
Wear that instead.

14:59.831 --> 15:01.581
Your dagger is right there.

15:03.541 --> 15:05.921
These clothes might be too big.

15:06.711 --> 15:09.091
These are the only men's clothes I have.

15:11.011 --> 15:13.851
Okay, sit down. You're hungry, right?

15:27.151 --> 15:30.151
You must have been starving.

15:30.241 --> 15:31.701
What's your name?

15:31.781 --> 15:33.071
Where did you come from?

15:33.781 --> 15:35.491
What happened to your family?

15:37.621 --> 15:40.871
See? He doesn't speak our language.

15:40.961 --> 15:42.791
Maybe he's a Dane.

15:42.871 --> 15:44.131
What are you trying to say?

15:45.211 --> 15:46.541
No matter where he's from,

15:46.631 --> 15:51.261
Jesus would never forgive me
for leaving an injured child lying there on the ground.

15:52.301 --> 15:53.471
But still,

15:53.551 --> 15:56.681
the Danes are the enemy of the English, right?

15:56.761 --> 16:01.271
Dad's serving in the military,
because the Danes attacked us.

16:02.441 --> 16:04.191
What's your point?

16:05.231 --> 16:09.981
Women and children are not obligated
to get involved in a quarrel among men.

16:10.071 --> 16:12.151
Maybe that's true, but still...

16:24.581 --> 16:26.211
He's covered in fleas.

16:26.291 --> 16:29.551
Stop scratching. They're getting in the food.

16:37.051 --> 16:38.511
See?

16:38.601 --> 16:40.601
Doesn't that feel better?

16:40.681 --> 16:44.351
Boys are such slobs.

16:44.441 --> 16:47.941
My youngest son used to scratch his head a lot too.

16:48.861 --> 16:51.991
Whenever he did that, I'd comb his hair.

16:54.821 --> 16:58.621
He caught a cold and died two years ago.

17:03.201 --> 17:05.461
I can't understand what you're saying.

17:08.211 --> 17:11.091
I'm not English.

17:16.681 --> 17:17.971
What?

17:18.051 --> 17:20.391
So, you can speak after all.

17:32.731 --> 17:34.491
Hey, woman.

17:34.571 --> 17:36.151
Yes? What is it?

17:36.701 --> 17:39.821
A Danish scout is hiding out in the area.

17:39.911 --> 17:42.241
Have you seen a suspicious-looking kid?

17:43.291 --> 17:46.161
A kid? You mean, a child pirate?

17:47.081 --> 17:48.671
Yes, but don't underestimate him.

17:48.751 --> 17:52.341
He killed two of His Highness' soldiers.

17:52.421 --> 17:54.881
He has an arrow wound on his left arm.

18:06.601 --> 18:09.901
Woman. Is that your kid?

18:09.981 --> 18:11.151
Yes, he is.

18:11.651 --> 18:14.401
He's my youngest, John. Is something wrong?

18:18.031 --> 18:20.991
He's the same height as that kid.

18:21.071 --> 18:22.621
If you see him, notify us.

18:32.791 --> 18:34.671
Do you understand what you're doing?

18:35.551 --> 18:37.421
He's a pirate.

18:37.881 --> 18:41.091
He killed two people. Even though he's only a kid.

18:41.181 --> 18:43.101
Why are you hiding him?

18:44.471 --> 18:47.641
It's not normal for a kid to be a pirate.

18:47.731 --> 18:49.191
Something must have happened.

18:49.731 --> 18:52.401
Something must have happened? So what?

18:52.481 --> 18:55.021
That's not what I'm talking about.

18:55.111 --> 18:58.191
He can't replace John.

19:02.571 --> 19:04.831
I'm going to go see the soldier.

19:18.591 --> 19:19.421
R--

19:20.341 --> 19:21.341
Run.

19:24.431 --> 19:25.721
Wait.

19:33.611 --> 19:34.611
John.

19:47.201 --> 19:48.911
Do you see a sign from Thorfinn?

19:49.001 --> 19:51.081
It should be coming any time now.

19:51.161 --> 19:52.001
I see it.

19:52.791 --> 19:53.831
Over there.

20:01.881 --> 20:02.841
There's a fire.

20:02.931 --> 20:04.761
The cottage on the beach is burning.

20:05.431 --> 20:07.141
Men. Come here.

20:07.221 --> 20:08.261
Hurry.

20:08.931 --> 20:10.931
Bring the buckets. The buckets.

20:23.201 --> 20:24.611
I knew it.

20:27.031 --> 20:29.081
So, you were disguising yourself.

20:37.421 --> 20:39.631
Hey. What's that?

20:43.801 --> 20:45.011
How terrible.

20:59.321 --> 21:00.151
Damn it.

21:00.531 --> 21:02.611
Who is that kid?

21:02.691 --> 21:04.401
Did he kill him?

21:21.091 --> 21:22.631
Why are you here?

21:22.711 --> 21:24.171
I told you to run away.

21:24.261 --> 21:26.181
I told you in English.

21:26.261 --> 21:27.181
He's coming this way.

21:28.051 --> 21:30.301
There's still time. Run to the forest.

21:30.391 --> 21:32.061
Get far away from the ocean.

21:32.141 --> 21:33.641
Hurry, or else they'll...

21:41.481 --> 21:43.441
Hey. What's that?

21:54.081 --> 21:55.461
No...

21:55.541 --> 21:56.961
Run.

21:57.621 --> 21:58.751
Forget about the fire.

21:59.461 --> 22:01.171
Everyone, run.

22:02.381 --> 22:05.591
The Vikings are here.

22:15.311 --> 22:17.771
Hey. Good job, Thorfinn.

22:18.561 --> 22:21.191
This village is doing better than I thought.

22:22.361 --> 22:24.191
Don't mess around.

22:24.281 --> 22:26.651
Finish them before the enemy arrives.
